function cipher takes string, rotate
	"This is a comment! a comment is also just a string expression by itself"
	"ciphered_string is an unset value that becomes a string when set"
	ciphered_string is ""
	"length is a standard library function"
	for i is 1 to length string
		"char_to_number is also a standard library function?"
		base_number is char_to_number "a"
		char_number is char_to_number string.i
		char_number is (char_number - base_number + rotate) mod 26 + base_number
		"number_to_char is a stdlib func"
		ciphered_string.i is number_to_char char_number
	return ciphered_string